sercontent.com/u/178451044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77","html_url":"https://github.com/adityajha77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T23:27:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T23:27:26Z","body":"hello @yusukebe \r\nYes, absolutely! Here are two common real-world use cases:\r\n\r\n1) +json media types: Modern APIs widely use standards like application/problem+json (RFC 7807 error responses) and application/vnd.api+json (JSON:API). Currently, prettyJSON skips formatting these responses during local debugging.\r\n2) Custom replacer: Useful for stringifying non-default types like BigInt or redacting sensitive fields (e.g. passwords/tokens) in dev logs.\r\nIt’s a lightweight, fully backward-compatible improvement that aligns prettyJSON with modern web standards!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287542856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287622511","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5226#issuecomment-5287622511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs