ps://api.github.com/users/codecov","html_url":"https://github.com/codecov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Codecov","description":"Codecov provides highly integrated tools to group, merge, archive and compare coverage reports. Whether your team is comparing changes in a pull request or reviewing a single commit, Codecov will improve the code review workflow and quality.\r\n\r\n## Code coverage done right.®\r\n\r\n1. Upload coverage reports from your CI builds.\r\n2. Codecov merges all builds and languages into one beautiful coherent report.\r\n3. Get commit statuses, pull request comments and coverage overlay via our browser extension.\r\n\r\nWhen Codecov merges your uploads it keeps track of the CI provider (inc. build details) and user specified context, e.g. `#unittest` ~ `#smoketest` or `#oldcode` ~ `#newcode`. You can track the `#unittest` coverage independently of other groups. [Learn more here](\r\nhttp://docs.codecov.io/docs/flags)\r\n\r\nThrough **Codecov's Browser Extension** reports overlay directly in GitHub UI to assist in code review in [Chrome](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/codecov/gedikamndpbemklijjkncpnolildpbgo) or Firefox (https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/codecov/)\r\n\r\n*Highly detailed* **pull request comments** and *customizable* **commit statuses** will improve your team's workflow and code coverage incrementally.\r\n\r\n**File backed configuration** all through the `codecov.yml`. \r\n\r\n## FAQ\r\n- Do you **merge multiple uploads** to the same commit? **Yes**\r\n- Do you **support multiple languages** in the same project? **Yes**\r\n- Can you **group coverage reports** by project and/or test type? **Yes**\r\n- How does **pricing** work? Only paid users can view reports and post statuses/comments. ","external_url":"https://codecov.io","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/codecov","created_at":"2016-09-25T14:18:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T19:12:59Z","permissions":{"administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"read","emails":"read","issues":"read","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["delete","fork","member","membership","organization","public","pull_request","push","release","repository","status","team_add"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287687308","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5226#issuecomment-5287687308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5226","id":5287687308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABOyu0jA","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T23:49:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T23:49:00Z","body":"@adityajha77 \r\n\r\nRegarding \"Custom replacer\", I don't think you have to do it in this middleware because the transaction is simple. What do you think of it? In the first place, I made this middleware just for debugging, as a super-simple use case. So, I don't want to add many functions. One question again: when did you face the need for this? What purpose and situation?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287687308/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287720180","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5226#issuecomment-5287720180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5226","id":5287720180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABOyw09A","user":{"login":"adityajha77","id":178451044,"node_id":"U_kgDOCqLyZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178451044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77","html_url":"https://github.com/adityajha77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adityajha77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T23:53:55Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T23:53:55Z","body":"Hi @yusukebe! Thanks for explaining your intent for `prettyJSON`.\r\n\r\nThat makes total sense—keeping `prettyJSON` super simple as a lightweight debugging helper aligns perfectly with Hono's philosophy. I completely agree with **dropping the `replacer` option** to avoid feature creep.\r\n\r\nTo answer your question about the situation for `+json` support:\r\n\r\n**Real-world situation:**\r\nI encountered this while debugging an API that returns standard error responses using RFC 7807 (`application/problem+json`). \r\n\r\nDuring local dev with `prettyJSON()` enabled:\r\n- Success responses (`application/json`) were pretty-printed in browser/curl logs.\r\n- Error responses (`application/problem+json`) remained minified on a single line because the `Content-Type` check only matched exact `application/json`.\r\n\r\nBy updating the `Content-Type` check to support `+json` subtypes, structured JSON error responses will be pretty-printed out-of-the-box during debugging, without adding any new options or API complexity.\r\n\r\nIs this ok that,\r\nI'll update the PR right away to remove `replacer` and keep this PR strictly focused on the small `+json` regex update!\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5287720180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/5296138330","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5226#issuecomment-5296138330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5226","id":5296138330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABO6yoWg","user":{"login":"adityajha77","id":178451044,"node_